      "worked_solution": "Since $m∠A=m∠C={45}^{∘}$ and $AB=BC,$ we have an isosceles right triangle. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14252107/assets/e13a301fe37d44657754877ef61b4d5e0e913c309784baa50d53f0d0e5edd913.png)\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {8}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 64 \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
